---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const apk = 'https://github.com/srjn45/warden-android-app/releases/latest/download/warden-latest.apk';
---
<section class="section android">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="android-title">Drive your fleet from your phone</h2>
    <p class="android-sub">
      A companion Android app for warden: spawn, watch, and talk to agents, with a
      full terminal and on-screen key bar. It connects to your own daemon over your
      LAN or a VPN such as Tailscale, using the same token auth as the web cockpit.
    </p>
    <div class="android-shots">
      <img src={`${base}media/warden-app-hosts.png`} alt="warden Android app — host picker and navigation" loading="lazy" />
      <img src={`${base}media/warden-app-agents.png`} alt="warden Android app — live agent list grouped by directory" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={apk}>Download the Android APK</a>
    </p>
    <p class="android-note">
      Sideload install: Android will ask you to allow installs from your browser
      the first time. That's expected. There is no Play Store listing yet. Prefer a
      browser? The web cockpit is mobile-responsive too.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
